This study reports the first observation of the semileptonic decays $ho^- 	o ho^- \ell^-  ar{
u}_\ell$ and $ ar{ho}^- 	o  ar{ho}^- \ell^-  ar{
u}_\ell$ via the corresponding charge-conjugate modes, utilizing a dataset of $4.5 	imes 10^9$ $J/\psi$ mesons collected by the BESIII experiment. The branching fractions were determined as $\mathcal{B}(ho^- 	o ho^- \ell^-  ar{
u}_\ell) = (3.09 \pm 0.45 \pm 0.92) 	imes 10^{-4}$ and $\mathcal{B}( ar{ho}^- 	o  ar{ho}^- \ell^-  ar{
u}_\ell) = (3.14 \pm 0.45 \pm 0.93) 	imes 10^{-4}$, where the uncertainties are statistical and systematic, respectively. The leading systematic uncertainty in these measurements stems from the normalization of the $J/\psi$ production cross-section.
